I recommend implementing encryption at rest with a reviewed design. Also, clear disclosures about platform backup controls are important since the app might depend on sandboxing and OS file encryption. I’m wondering if we should prioritize this, given the security risk is not well-defined, yet sensitive data might be exposed in plaintext SQL. Perhaps we can categorize severity using a High/Medium scheme for clarity. Other factors like app permissions and untrusted imported content also need attention."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Reviewing CDN and policy findings**

It seems the CDN likely logs page visits, which I need to inspect, especially concerning the static page CSS and GitHub Pages policies. Users can email for any inquiries, and “git status” appears normal. I also see the P3-5 report is still open, which should note preexisting findings as we conduct the audit. Perhaps the new policy will address this when updated, but details around provider retention remain unresolved—definitely something to keep in mind!"}]}

