DEVELOPMENT.md:65:Android Auto Backup stays on, but it must never carry private content off the device. The app owns the backup rules: `plugins/withAndroidBackupRules.js` writes the rule files during prebuild and sets them in the manifest. The rules back up shared preferences only, without the encrypted `SecureStore` preferences. They exclude the database directory (`SQLite/`), `media/`, and `drafts/`. The `expo-secure-store` plugin runs with `configureAndroidBackup: false`, so no other plugin can replace these rules silently.
